  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU through the ModBus communication board: address by DIP switches 1-8, 9600 or 19200 bit/s (switch 9), no or even parity (switch 10).",
    "Addresses are the manual's Modicon numbers without the leading digit (input register 30009 is input register 9), counted from 1 (address_base 1).",
    "Temperatures are degrees Celsius x 10 (683 = 68.3 °C). Values the BAS writes (holding registers 40002 and up) are only used when the matching configuration bit in 40001 is set, and must be refreshed within the ModBus timer set on the unit.",
    "Status, blocking and lockout codes (input registers 30014-30016) are listed in the troubleshooting chapter of the manual.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
